# requires.psv -- what a program needs that the card cannot see for itself:
# a Microware module the DEPENDS scan and the cio star do not record, another
# program, or a shell.  name|requirement|where it is stated.  The card lists
# the requirement under Needs.  Every line comes from a document on the disk
# or a measurement written down elsewhere -- never from a guess.  A module the
# collection does not carry is named plainly as something the reader's own
# OS-9 system provides.
a2p|perl, to run the script it writes|SRC/perl4/README-OSK; tools/datatests/perl.cases
perl|a shell named by SHELL for system, backticks and piped opens (SYS/login sets ksh)|SRC/perl4/README-OSK
lua|Microware's csl (on this disk)|SOURCES.txt, lua 3.0 section
tterm|Microware's csl (on this disk), and fpu on a machine without a 68881|DOC/comms/readme
tsu|Microware's csl (on this disk), and fpu on a machine without a 68881|DOC/comms/readme
xyt|Microware's csl (on this disk), and fpu on a machine without a 68881|DOC/comms/readme
gzip68k_csl|Microware's csl (on this disk)|DOC/INDEX
gzip020_csl|Microware's csl (on this disk)|DOC/INDEX
gzipcpu32k_csl|Microware's csl (on this disk)|DOC/INDEX
